  "_notes": [
    "The season data file's votingHistory episode 11 entry lists 'eliminated: Ryan', but the vote tally in that same entry (Kitty 3, Brody 2, Ryan 2, Geoff 1, Mickey 1) plus the placements array's notes for both Kitty ('Voted out Episode 11 (3-2-2-1-1) to RI') and Ryan ('Voted out Episode 12 (5-2-1) to Redemption') plus the chronicle's own episode 11 and 12 narration all agree Kitty was voted out in episode 11 and Ryan in episode 12. Treated 'eliminated: Ryan' on the episode-11 entry as a data file labeling error and used Kitty for episode 11 / Ryan for episode 12 accordingly.",
    "One extraction pass over the chronicle's episode 12 text reported a Redemption Island duel loss ('Puppet Master') for a player named 'Dwayne.' This is inconsistent with both the data file's authoritative placement notes (Dwayne was 'Directly eliminated at merge (4-3-3-1)' in episode 9, with no Redemption Island note) and the chronicle's own episode 9 narration, which explicitly states Dwayne's merge boot used no Redemption Island pipeline. Treated as a chronicle continuity/transcription error and not reflected in Dwayne's record. Emma's confirmed Redemption Island duel loss ('Block It Out', episode 13) and Kitty's confirmed Redemption Island duel loss ('House of Cards', episode 14) were used instead, which is consistent with their relative placement ordering (Ryan 8th > Emma 10th > Kitty 9th... note Kitty placement 9 is actually ranked above Emma's 10, but eliminated later per the duel-loss episode ordering used here: Emma ep13, Kitty ep14 — both are later than Dwayne's ep9 merge boot either way).",
    "No showmances/romantic pairings were found anywhere in the chronicle text for this season; the various named 'Blood vs. Water' duos (Surfers Bros, Sis4ever, AnxietyBro, Sponsor Chasers, Ice Partners, Fighters For Love, Brainiacs, Fantasy Duo, Dad and Son, Gothic Hearts) are pre-existing real-life partner/family/friend pairs per the season's twist premise, not in-game romances, so they were recorded as alliance/ally relationships rather than showmances.",
    "No eliminations across the season's 17 episodes were described by the chronicle using explicit blindside/shock/ambush language, with two exceptions: Geoff's episode 13 boot (explicitly framed as Blaineley betraying an 'unbreakable' bond, 'unbreakable doesn't mean unbetrayable') and Brody's episode 14 boot (explicitly framed as 'betrayal with a receipt' after Kelly bonded with him then voted him out same episode). All other eliminations were narrated as consensus votes, Redemption Island duel losses, rock draws, idol-negation math, or medical evacuation, without shock/ambush framing, so 'blindsided' was left false for those players per the brief's instruction not to infer blindsides from placement or vote splits alone.",
    "votesAgainstTotal for each player was taken from the season data file's 'votesReceived' field (already an authoritative aggregate of the same votingHistory), rather than manually re-summed from chronicle prose, to avoid transcription drift; it is consistent with every per-episode tally the chronicle extraction surfaced."
  ]
